<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index up 0.41 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index up 0.41 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 0.25 points, 0.41 percent, to 61.59 points after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index fell 12.04 points to a provisional 2,814.16.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 13.42 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
